```
NORTHBOUND     UI / NOC / CSR / External APIs
               REST / GraphQL / gRPC
                    │
             AGENT / COGNITION
             AGENT CONTROL          multi-turn · ownership · routing
             EXECUTION CONTROL      ledger · authority · idempotency · approvals
             ACTION LAYER
                    │
SOUTHBOUND     REST / gRPC / MQ / NETCONF / gNMI
               BSS / OSS / NETWORK
```

Keep five instincts from that drawing.

- Cognition does not touch the network. Execution is a choke point.
- Ownership and routing are first-class. NOC, CSR, and APIs will contend for the same objects.
- Ledger and idempotency sit above adapters, not inside a vendor client.
- Approvals belong with execution, not with the chatbot.
- Southbound protocol diversity is acknowledged instead of wished away.

What it lacked is the rest of a production OSS: a closed loop, shared state, an east-west plane, risk class, human takeover as protocol, and an honest home for ontology, grounding, models — and for Source of Truth versus System of Record.

