This is materially different from saying the pod “implements L1-L6.”

### Modern example — RAN energy management

RAN energy management is a useful current example because the decision surface is probabilistic and dynamic while the network mutation must remain tightly controlled.

O-RAN energy-saving work includes techniques such as **Cell and Carrier Shutdown**, **RF Channel Reconfiguration**, and energy optimization across O-RU and O-Cloud resources. O-RAN places longer-horizon AI/ML optimization in the **SMO / Non-RT RIC with rApps** and near-real-time adjustments in the **Near-RT RIC with xApps**. The reference architecture can sit above or alongside those mechanisms without replacing their domain control loops.

