## Layers

**Northbound is intake, not intelligence.** Same transports are fine. The contracts are not.

| ActorNeedsMust not get |                                          |                            |
| ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |
| UI                     | Multi-turn, citations, draft plans       | Raw device verbs as the UX |
| NOC                    | Blast radius, evidence, pause / rollback | Unexplained autonomy       |
| CSR                    | Customer-safe outcomes                   | CLI, topology internals    |
| External API           | Schema, idempotency key, SLA             | Conversational ambiguity   |
| Peer agent             | A2A task + reservation                   | Free-text as a lock        |

**Cognition is the probabilistic reasoning boundary.** The runtime that hosts it is pluggable. LangGraph, OpenAI Agents SDK, Google ADK, a Bot0-native runtime, or another framework may run individual agents or coordinate multi-agent reasoning. These runtimes may retrieve, ground, plan, critique, ask, delegate, hand off, and maintain local conversational/task state. They do not acquire write authority merely because they orchestrate the agents. Cognition may retrieve, ask, draft, explain, and propose. It may not hold unrestricted southbound credentials and it may not commit outside Execution Control. Output intended for execution is a typed plan whose nouns resolve to ontology types and live instance ids.

**Agent Control is conversation and contention.** Session, owner, route to the right specialist graph, lock, handoff, preempt. Two agents do not write the same circuit. A smarter plan does not beat an existing owner.

**Execution Control is the kernel.** Authority scoped to object class × domain × verb × time. Risk class and change window. Dry-run before commit. Policy engine first, human second. Idempotency keys from the caller and internally for every mutation. Pause, escalate, rollback, compensate as verbs. Execution does not care which model proposed the plan. It re-grounds against live knowledge at commit time.

**Action is protocol truth.** Map ontology objects onto TMF, YANG, vendor dialects, queues. Diffs, commit/abort, compensation when the protocol cannot give a real transaction. If Action is “the LLM picked a tool,” the architecture has already failed.

**Southbound is BSS, OSS, and the network as they are.** Results climb back. HTTP 200 is not success. Observed state versus intent is success.

