## Ontology and grounding

**Ontology lives in Knowledge.** Types, verbs, relations, constraints — TMF SID / Intent Ontology, 3GPP NRM, YANG, plus local extensions. One model of the world. Not a second “LLM ontology.”

Consumed in four places, copied in none of them:

- Cognition emits only ontology-shaped plans.
- Agent Control locks by type and instance.
- Execution allow-lists verbs on types and assigns risk from those verbs.
- Action projects those types onto protocols.

**Grounding is the join**, not a box. It turns “the PE in Dallas that’s flapping” into Resource\:PE-DAL-01, type ProviderEdge, site DAL-1, port xe-0/0/3, in-flight change CHG-9921.

It runs three times: inbound utterance → typed intent; plan time, every entity must resolve or the step is illegal; pre-commit, Execution re-grounds against live SoT so the plan cannot fire on a renamed object. The model proposes mentions. The SoT accepts or rejects. Invented IDs mean grounding failed.

